1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,795
[BILLY]<i> I don't want</i>
<i>our efforts to go to waste.</i>

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:05,338
<i>Mission accomplished, dude.</i>

3
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:07,674
<i>I got his location!</i>

4
00:00:07,757 --> 00:00:10,176
[BILLY] <i>I'm outside the troll's house.</i>

5
00:00:10,260 --> 00:00:11,553
[JORDAN] <i>That's dangerous!</i>

6
00:00:11,636 --> 00:00:12,679
[CALOY] <i>Who's there?</i>

7
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,514
- [CALOY] <i>Hey!</i>
- [BILLY]<i> Who's giving you those orders?</i>

8
00:00:14,597 --> 00:00:16,057
[CALOY]<i> Why would I tell you?</i>
<i>Ms. Cariño.</i>

9
00:00:16,141 --> 00:00:17,434
<i>Help!</i>

10
00:00:17,976 --> 00:00:19,352
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]
- [CALOY] <i>Who are you?!</i>

11
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:21,020
[GRUNTS]

12
00:00:22,355 --> 00:00:23,982
[GRUNTS]

13
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,650
- [GROANS]
- [KNIFE SWISHES]

14
00:00:25,734 --> 00:00:28,319
- [BILLY]<i> Auntie Pres?</i>
- [PRECIOUS]<i> Oh, Billy?</i>

15
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:29,821
[PRECIOUS] <i>We have a visitor.</i>

16
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:32,323
<i>- Ms. Billy!</i>
- [BILLY]<i> Abi!</i>

17
00:00:32,407 --> 00:00:33,867
<i>I wanted to thank you</i>

18
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:37,787
<i>because our conversation</i>
<i>really helped me a lot.</i>

19
00:00:47,630 --> 00:00:54,220
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

20
00:00:57,849 --> 00:00:59,309
JESSIE: YOU'RE TRENDING!
COLLAB SOON

21
00:01:01,936 --> 00:01:07,734
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

22
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,155
[LINE RINGING]

23
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:13,406
Hello?

24
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,785
Do something.

25
00:01:18,328 --> 00:01:19,913
If not, you'll get dragged into this.

26
00:01:22,290 --> 00:01:23,750
I don't want to go to jail again.

27
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:25,543
I've been here numerous times.

28
00:01:27,921 --> 00:01:34,594
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

29
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,719
Your temperature's very high.

30
00:02:17,887 --> 00:02:19,139
You okay?

31
00:02:19,848 --> 00:02:21,182
I am completely fine.

32
00:02:22,767 --> 00:02:25,979
Stop saying you're okay. You're not okay.

33
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:27,355
Okay.

34
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:30,275
Time to drink. Sorry, sit up.

35
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,402
One, two, three, okay.

36
00:02:32,485 --> 00:02:33,570
- [GRUNTS]
- Sorry.

37
00:02:34,362 --> 00:02:36,489
Here. Give me your hand.

38
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:41,828
["KULIMLIM" BY ANGELA KEN PLAYING]

39
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:43,079
Okay.

40
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,498
If you're still not feeling well tomorrow,

41
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,292
I'll take you to the hospital, okay?

42
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:48,251
[JORDAN EXHALES]

43
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,545
- All right.
- Okay.

44
00:02:50,628 --> 00:02:52,171
[SETS CUPS DOWN]

45
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,883
Move a bit, sorry.

46
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:56,009
[JORDAN HUMS]

47
00:02:58,845 --> 00:03:05,685
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

48
00:03:14,944 --> 00:03:21,951
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

49
00:03:36,966 --> 00:03:43,932
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

50
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:05,912
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

51
00:04:20,593 --> 00:04:26,099
["KULIMLIM" CONTINUES]

52
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:36,776
[SOFT GRUNT]

53
00:04:38,695 --> 00:04:42,865
- Good morning, Billy!
- Good morning, naughty boy.

54
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:43,866
[BILLY GROANS]

55
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:46,995
- Billy. Why'd you sleep here?
- Hm?

56
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:48,830
I wonder why.

57
00:04:48,913 --> 00:04:51,165
Just because. I just missed you.

58
00:04:51,249 --> 00:04:53,126
Am I not allowed in here anymore?

59
00:04:53,209 --> 00:04:55,586
- You're still allowed!
- I'm still allowed? Okay.

60
00:04:57,046 --> 00:04:57,922
[BILLY GROANS]

61
00:04:58,006 --> 00:05:00,508
I saw this last night. What's this?

62
00:05:00,591 --> 00:05:03,886
I want to fix my school grades.

63
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:07,598
I heard it's hard
to get into those schools.

64
00:05:08,558 --> 00:05:11,477
- College universities?
- Yes.

65
00:05:11,561 --> 00:05:13,313
But it's still too early for this.

66
00:05:14,814 --> 00:05:17,066
What do they say is the best school?

67
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,444
It's there in California!

68
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:21,863
The University of Kingsley.

69
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:25,533
That's the best school
for software engineering!

70
00:05:25,616 --> 00:05:28,411
- Hmm!
- But…

71
00:05:28,494 --> 00:05:30,204
It's too expensive.

72
00:05:31,039 --> 00:05:32,665
I could study here too.

73
00:05:32,749 --> 00:05:36,294
There are also many Philippine schools
that offer software engineering.

74
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:39,380
I have my top three schools I can go to.

75
00:05:39,464 --> 00:05:41,466
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

76
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:43,801
University of Kingsley.

77
00:05:44,552 --> 00:05:47,305
Noted. Okay, you'll study here.

78
00:05:47,972 --> 00:05:49,432
- Really, Billy?
- Mm-hmm!

79
00:05:49,515 --> 00:05:50,683
- Sure?
- Mm-hmm!

80
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:53,061
- Promise?
- Promise.

81
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:56,564
I'm going to study well,
so your efforts won't go to waste.

82
00:05:56,647 --> 00:05:58,066
When I graduate,

83
00:05:58,149 --> 00:06:01,527
you can stop working,
so you can finally rest.

84
00:06:01,611 --> 00:06:05,323
You know I'd do anything for you, right?

85
00:06:05,406 --> 00:06:07,784
That's okay. I love you.

86
00:06:08,367 --> 00:06:10,078
I love you, Billy.
Thank you for everything.

87
00:06:10,161 --> 00:06:15,500
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:20,046
Are our quick response templates
for LoveLine ready?

89
00:06:20,129 --> 00:06:21,881
- Yes, chief.
- Okay, good.

90
00:06:21,964 --> 00:06:24,383
Please remind the Ads Team
that we have to be ready

91
00:06:24,467 --> 00:06:26,177
by next week for the push campaign.

92
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:27,386
- [BLAIRE] Okay.
- Thank you.

93
00:06:27,470 --> 00:06:30,014
- How's Jordan?
- Is he still alive?

94
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:32,058
Calm down. He's fine now.

95
00:06:32,141 --> 00:06:34,102
- Ahh…
- [MARJ] That's good.

96
00:06:34,185 --> 00:06:36,479
I plan to vlog
about everything that happened.

97
00:06:36,562 --> 00:06:37,939
Let's repost it,

98
00:06:38,022 --> 00:06:41,150
so we can push the fact that
you're the real victim.

99
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,237
Speaking of pushing…

100
00:06:45,446 --> 00:06:48,116
The equipment's getting delivered.

101
00:06:48,199 --> 00:06:52,286
They're already charging me
for the remaining balance of our payment.

102
00:06:54,122 --> 00:06:55,915
Will we still push through with it?

103
00:06:55,998 --> 00:06:59,418
I mean, the price of the equipment,

104
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:03,840
the additional manpower, the new gadgets,

105
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:06,259
and the software is no joke.

106
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:08,553
My crystals can't take this anymore.

107
00:07:08,636 --> 00:07:10,972
Ralph's friends with the supplier.

108
00:07:11,055 --> 00:07:12,932
Maybe he can discuss a refund.

109
00:07:13,015 --> 00:07:16,060
No. I'll finance this.

110
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:19,147
This can't not push through just because--

111
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,356
Of her.

112
00:07:21,774 --> 00:07:26,779
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

113
00:07:26,863 --> 00:07:28,197
Billy, can we talk?

114
00:07:32,368 --> 00:07:34,370
I hate to admit this, but…

115
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:38,291
I realized that I'm acting pathetic.

116
00:07:38,374 --> 00:07:40,042
I mean,

117
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:41,544
with my beauty,

118
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,965
I'm acting crazy running after a guy
that doesn't even like me.

119
00:07:46,048 --> 00:07:47,842
So what are you doing here?

120
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:51,846
Are you here
because you're feeling guilty?

121
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,683
Are you confessing
that you ordered Carlos Toledo

122
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:58,060
to destroy my company?

123
00:07:59,020 --> 00:08:01,355
You're acting guilty now
because Jordan got involved.

124
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:02,273
Is that it?

125
00:08:04,317 --> 00:08:05,818
[VALERIE SIGHS]

126
00:08:05,902 --> 00:08:06,861
Billy.

127
00:08:09,030 --> 00:08:11,949
I may be desperate to win Jordan back,

128
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:13,618
but you know me.

129
00:08:13,701 --> 00:08:16,829
I can destroy someone
if I want to destroy them.

130
00:08:16,913 --> 00:08:20,291
But I won't go as low and as far
as working with criminals.

131
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:23,085
And spray paint a car?

132
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:25,379
Do you really think I would do that?

133
00:08:26,923 --> 00:08:27,965
[VALERIE SIGHS]

134
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:30,593
I'm here because I wanna help you guys.

135
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:32,762
And I wanna make it up to Jordan.

136
00:08:32,845 --> 00:08:39,644
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

137
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:44,106
Guys, let's be real.

138
00:08:44,190 --> 00:08:46,609
We all know that fake news is everywhere.

139
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:49,320
And, sadly,

140
00:08:49,946 --> 00:08:53,783
recently, Ms. Billy Cariño, LoveList CEO,

141
00:08:53,866 --> 00:08:55,618
has fallen victim to one.

142
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:58,329
Someone's trying to destroy her company,

143
00:08:58,412 --> 00:09:00,248
and we're not buying it.

144
00:09:00,331 --> 00:09:02,542
You guys might be wondering,

145
00:09:02,625 --> 00:09:05,753
"Why are you on her side?
Don't you have beef with each other?"

146
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:09,590
Well, yeah, but that's a different story.

147
00:09:09,674 --> 00:09:14,345
With this topic, I want you to hear it
straight from the source.

148
00:09:14,428 --> 00:09:17,306
Here to spill, Ms. Billy Cariño.

149
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,307
Thank you.

150
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,103
This isn't just an ordinary issue.

151
00:09:22,186 --> 00:09:23,479
This is a crime.

152
00:09:25,606 --> 00:09:29,068
I don't know who they are,
what it was for,

153
00:09:29,151 --> 00:09:33,656
or why they even went so far
as to hire a hacker troll.

154
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:36,993
But the good news is,
that hacker is now in jail.

155
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:40,621
And when we found them, they said

156
00:09:40,705 --> 00:09:43,791
that they don't know
who commissioned them.

157
00:09:43,874 --> 00:09:45,668
They were just paid to do it.

158
00:09:46,711 --> 00:09:50,423
People might think that this is
just a petty cyberwar.

159
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:54,093
But this is a serious matter to us.

160
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:58,848
I think everyone knows
what happened to my friend,

161
00:09:58,931 --> 00:10:01,726
the Tech Lead of LoveList,
Jordan Valentin.

162
00:10:03,811 --> 00:10:05,771
Jordan is okay now.

163
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,732
But what we're not okay with

164
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:11,235
is how we still can't track down
the mastermind behind this.

165
00:10:13,571 --> 00:10:17,825
The reason I'm here right now
is because we need your help.

166
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:20,286
If you know anything

167
00:10:20,369 --> 00:10:23,414
or if you have any kind of information
that can help with our case,

168
00:10:23,497 --> 00:10:26,375
please, don't hesitate to reach out.

169
00:10:27,501 --> 00:10:29,045
[BILLY] <i>Moving forward,</i>

170
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,589
<i>I just want to let you all know</i>

171
00:10:31,672 --> 00:10:34,175
<i>that this setback won't stop LoveList.</i>

172
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:36,510
At the end of the day,

173
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:38,929
the responsibilities of LoveList

174
00:10:39,013 --> 00:10:41,682
are conveyed clearly to its users.

175
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:43,059
[BILLY] <i>And with that,</i>

176
00:10:43,851 --> 00:10:46,771
<i>we will push through with</i>
<i>our plans for LoveList,</i>

177
00:10:46,854 --> 00:10:48,981
<i>and that includes LoveLine.</i>

178
00:10:49,065 --> 00:10:53,069
Because I believe that the truth
always has its way

179
00:10:53,152 --> 00:10:55,029
of revealing itself.

180
00:10:55,112 --> 00:10:56,155
And love?

181
00:10:57,156 --> 00:10:58,282
Love always wins.

182
00:11:00,660 --> 00:11:04,080
So whoever you are
who's trying to mess with us,

183
00:11:04,955 --> 00:11:06,624
<i>no matter where you are,</i>

184
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,252
<i>I'll find you.</i>

185
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:16,342
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

186
00:11:16,425 --> 00:11:17,968
[TENSE MUSIC FADES]

187
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:21,305
Gosh, my followers will love this!

188
00:11:22,223 --> 00:11:24,683
Hey, guys! Right now, we're in Ja--

189
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:27,144
Hi! Hi, guys!

190
00:11:27,228 --> 00:11:28,979
Uh, isn't this my content?

191
00:11:29,063 --> 00:11:31,065
This isn't supposed to be for you to post!

192
00:11:31,148 --> 00:11:34,276
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE] This is an exclusive!

193
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,613
Just kidding! She's getting pissed.

194
00:11:37,696 --> 00:11:38,864
You're getting pissed!

195
00:11:38,948 --> 00:11:40,324
It won't be an exclusive anymore.

196
00:11:40,408 --> 00:11:42,159
My fans might get sick of it.

197
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,703
They're so over our drama.

198
00:11:44,787 --> 00:11:46,622
All right, go ahead. Continue. [GIGGLES]

199
00:11:47,248 --> 00:11:49,542
Okay… let's go over there!

200
00:11:50,084 --> 00:11:52,253
Wait, this one's exclusive.

201
00:11:52,336 --> 00:11:54,213
Exclusively mine. [GIGGLES]

202
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:55,965
- I'm all yours, baby.
- Aw!

203
00:11:56,048 --> 00:11:58,175
Wow! How sweet!

204
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,844
Let's move on to these two!

205
00:11:59,927 --> 00:12:01,137
[BOTH CLEARING THROATS]

206
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:04,014
Of course, he's all mine too! [GIGGLING]

207
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:05,224
Of course!

208
00:12:05,307 --> 00:12:07,017
- Hi!
- Hi!

209
00:12:07,101 --> 00:12:08,352
Hey, what the?!

210
00:12:08,436 --> 00:12:11,272
Oh, no, I was just stretching my neck…

211
00:12:11,355 --> 00:12:12,773
- Do you know her?
- Oh, no…

212
00:12:12,857 --> 00:12:15,192
Hey, bro!
[NERVOUS CHUCKLE] Hey!

213
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,778
- Let's go, Toni. [CHUCKLING]
- She's not even that pretty.

214
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:21,532
By the way, Marj, have you
already chosen someone?

215
00:12:21,615 --> 00:12:23,409
- You have two matches, right?
- Hmm… [CLICKS TONGUE]

216
00:12:23,492 --> 00:12:26,704
The right one at the right time,
as they say, right?

217
00:12:26,787 --> 00:12:29,331
I agree. Love at the right time!

218
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:30,416
- Mm-hmm.
- Mm-hmm!

219
00:12:30,499 --> 00:12:33,627
- Okay! Bye, guys!
- Bye!

220
00:12:33,711 --> 00:12:34,962
[MARJ GIGGLING]

221
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:36,964
That's right. Love at the right time!

222
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:39,133
Drinks! Drinks for everyone!

223
00:12:39,216 --> 00:12:42,970
Wow, you're acting as if
you're in a relationship!

224
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:46,182
Well, I did say
love at the right time, didn't I?

225
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:47,433
He's right.

226
00:12:47,516 --> 00:12:49,143
You know what, I agree.

227
00:12:49,226 --> 00:12:51,395
Love at the right time.

228
00:12:51,479 --> 00:12:53,022
And guess what?

229
00:12:53,105 --> 00:12:55,149
I think it's almost time.

230
00:12:55,941 --> 00:12:57,318
- Okay!
- [LAUGHTER]

231
00:12:57,401 --> 00:12:59,445
- We'll just make our rounds.
- Sure!

232
00:13:02,114 --> 00:13:09,038
[DIGITAL TRILLING]

233
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:16,086
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

234
00:13:20,591 --> 00:13:23,177
Billy, thank you so much for accepting me

235
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:25,221
to be a part of the LoveList family.

236
00:13:25,304 --> 00:13:28,432
I'm so excited to be
your honorary consultant.

237
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:29,850
[LAUGHS]

238
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:31,101
Anyways,

239
00:13:31,185 --> 00:13:34,480
I think that me and Marj
will have a good working chemistry.

240
00:13:34,563 --> 00:13:36,565
I hope she learns a lot from me.

241
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:37,983
[LAUGHS]

242
00:13:38,692 --> 00:13:39,777
Cheers!

243
00:13:40,444 --> 00:13:41,529
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

244
00:13:41,612 --> 00:13:44,323
- [BOTTLES CLINKING]
- Cheers!

245
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:47,034
Welcome to the LoveList family, Val.

246
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:48,744
- Cheers?
- [VALERIE] Cheers.

247
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,079
[BILLY GIGGLES]

248
00:13:50,955 --> 00:13:51,997
[THUDS]

249
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:54,124
I'll just go to the restroom.

250
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:57,044
Mmm. Take a seat.

251
00:13:57,127 --> 00:13:58,128
I'll just sit for a bit.

252
00:13:58,212 --> 00:14:02,091
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

253
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:05,928
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

254
00:14:06,011 --> 00:14:07,179
[THUDDING]

255
00:14:07,263 --> 00:14:08,973
I thought you were going to the restroom?

256
00:14:09,807 --> 00:14:11,517
Girl… what is it?

257
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:12,893
What do you mean?

258
00:14:12,977 --> 00:14:14,311
I can sense it.

259
00:14:14,395 --> 00:14:15,396
Just spill it.

260
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:16,855
Okay, fine.

261
00:14:17,815 --> 00:14:19,441
- I'll be honest, okay?
- Mm-hmm.

262
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:24,697
If it's just damage control,
I can do it too.

263
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:28,158
The interview
that Valerie did on her vlog?

264
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:29,869
I can do that!

265
00:14:29,952 --> 00:14:31,787
Do you have five million subscribers?

266
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:33,372
Exactly.

267
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:36,876
Marj, you cannot argue with success, okay?

268
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:40,254
Just look at the impact of Val's vlog.

269
00:14:40,337 --> 00:14:43,048
LoveList's membership shot back up again.

270
00:14:44,091 --> 00:14:45,301
It's that easy?

271
00:14:45,384 --> 00:14:47,511
Just because of that,
she gets to be a part of us?

272
00:14:47,595 --> 00:14:50,139
She's a content creator now too?

273
00:14:50,222 --> 00:14:51,682
Wow!

274
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:54,935
Does our chief really believe
that she's innocent?

275
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:00,024
Next time, if you have questions,

276
00:15:00,107 --> 00:15:01,942
go to me directly.

277
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:05,362
It's better for me if we communicate more.

278
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:07,865
Sorry, chief.

279
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:10,910
It's just that…

280
00:15:11,911 --> 00:15:14,455
things are happening way too fast.

281
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:17,917
Like, honestly, I can't keep up.

282
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,209
Like how…

283
00:15:19,793 --> 00:15:21,921
how sure are we that Valerie
has nothing to do

284
00:15:22,004 --> 00:15:23,672
with the sabotage?

285
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:26,675
I am for peace, Marj.

286
00:15:26,759 --> 00:15:30,095
Didn't Valerie tell us that
she's got nothing to do with it?

287
00:15:30,179 --> 00:15:33,265
Then I want to give her
the benefit of the doubt.

288
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,726
Now, I won't say
she completely has my trust.

289
00:15:35,809 --> 00:15:37,478
She still has to work for it.

290
00:15:38,395 --> 00:15:40,773
We're on the same page, okay?

291
00:15:40,856 --> 00:15:44,944
So, trust me, relax,
and let's enjoy the night.

292
00:15:45,945 --> 00:15:47,029
- Cheers?
- Cheers!

293
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,822
- [GIGGLING] Cheers!
- Cheers!

294
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,866
- [TONI GIGGLING] Just chill.
- Sorry. [GIGGLING]

295
00:15:51,533 --> 00:15:52,493
Val!

296
00:15:54,745 --> 00:15:56,956
Hey, thanks for helping us at the company.

297
00:15:57,539 --> 00:15:58,958
Thank you too.

298
00:16:00,084 --> 00:16:02,878
I know you're the reason
why Billy accepted me

299
00:16:02,962 --> 00:16:04,213
into your team.

300
00:16:07,299 --> 00:16:09,635
I just wanted to clear the air between us.

301
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:11,553
You know,

302
00:16:11,637 --> 00:16:13,347
we go way back after all.

303
00:16:14,515 --> 00:16:16,725
Hey, don't get any ideas.

304
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:20,270
As much as I want to say that
I'm doing this for you,

305
00:16:20,354 --> 00:16:22,356
that's really not the case.

306
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:24,566
The truth is,

307
00:16:25,317 --> 00:16:27,277
I'm doing this for myself.

308
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,737
For my peace of mind.

309
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:30,781
Okay.

310
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:32,408
Good.

311
00:16:34,910 --> 00:16:39,665
- [DIGITAL TRILLING]
- [FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

312
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:44,753
- Auntie Pres!
- Whoa! Hey!

313
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:46,005
- Oh my gosh!
- Hey, give it back!

314
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:50,092
- Oh, thank you, Lord!
- What're you thanking Him for?

315
00:16:50,175 --> 00:16:51,885
- What're you on?
- Auntie Pres!

316
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:53,053
Is this a blessing or what?

317
00:16:53,137 --> 00:16:55,222
Wait a minute, hold it.
Let me make it clear.

318
00:16:55,305 --> 00:16:57,224
- I only downloaded this…
- Mm-hmm?

319
00:16:57,307 --> 00:17:01,395
…because… uh,
you guys need extra members.

320
00:17:01,478 --> 00:17:03,230
- I just helped out. Charity!
- Okay!

321
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:05,441
You're really going to lie to me?

322
00:17:05,524 --> 00:17:08,110
I monitor all of the sign-ups.

323
00:17:08,193 --> 00:17:09,194
- Hmm.
- Hmm?

324
00:17:09,278 --> 00:17:10,821
Give it to me. Let me see.

325
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:12,239
Just let me take a peek.

326
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,117
Brandon!

327
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:17,578
Wow! It's a 97% match!

328
00:17:17,661 --> 00:17:19,621
This is really high, Auntie.

329
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:21,206
Ooh…

330
00:17:21,915 --> 00:17:23,917
- How about it? Want to give it a try?
- Huh?

331
00:17:24,668 --> 00:17:25,878
- Go for it. Accept it.
- Huh?

332
00:17:25,961 --> 00:17:27,713
- Here. Press it.
- I might press it by accident!

333
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:29,715
- Just accept it!
- No, I won't accept it!

334
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:31,800
- You-- I'm not sure about this.
- You don't want to?

335
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:32,926
No, I--

336
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:34,344
Okay.

337
00:17:34,428 --> 00:17:36,680
I'm not sure if I'm ready yet

338
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:39,683
because maybe I still haven't
moved on from my husband,

339
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:40,934
so, no.

340
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:42,144
- Let's leave it at that.
- Uh-huh…

341
00:17:42,227 --> 00:17:44,980
- Let's leave it.
- There's only one way to find out!

342
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:47,191
- [PRECIOUS FAKE SOBBING]
- Uncle Rico is already smiling

343
00:17:47,274 --> 00:17:48,650
down from heaven.

344
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:50,652
It's been a few years since then too.

345
00:17:50,736 --> 00:17:52,446
- Okay, uh…
- Mm-hmm.

346
00:17:52,529 --> 00:17:55,532
Billy, let me just tell you that Rico

347
00:17:56,658 --> 00:18:00,871
had a heart attack on the very day
of our wedding, okay?

348
00:18:00,954 --> 00:18:02,748
I'm scared that it'll happen again!

349
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:04,500
- I don't want that.
- It won't happen again.

350
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,501
God is gracious.

351
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:08,045
He'll give you a second, third,
and even fourth chance.

352
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,672
- And now, it's your chance!
- [SHRIEKS]

353
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:12,382
- No! No!
- Come on!

354
00:18:12,466 --> 00:18:15,469
But, wait, what do you--?
Why is it my chance?

355
00:18:15,552 --> 00:18:18,680
- What do you mean?
- Why don't you give yourself a chance?

356
00:18:18,764 --> 00:18:19,723
Why me and not you?

357
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:23,977
Oh, no, chances come by,
and mine hasn't arrived yet.

358
00:18:24,061 --> 00:18:26,396
- But yours is already here.
- Oh, really? [LAUGHING]

359
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:28,649
- It's one click away!
- [LAUGHING] No!

360
00:18:28,732 --> 00:18:30,234
No, no, no!

361
00:18:30,317 --> 00:18:31,902
Honey, there's no chance anyone's coming.

362
00:18:31,985 --> 00:18:33,779
Besides, it's already 10:00 p.m.

363
00:18:33,862 --> 00:18:37,574
- [YAWNS] Oh, I'm getting sleepy!
- You're getting sleepy?

364
00:18:37,658 --> 00:18:39,284
- Let's go to bed.
- Come on.

365
00:18:39,368 --> 00:18:41,620
Because<i></i>LoveLine launches tomorrow.

366
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:43,330
- Tomorrow!
- I'll be there, yes.

367
00:18:43,413 --> 00:18:45,207
Don't cook. Let's eat out afterward.

368
00:18:45,290 --> 00:18:47,042
Huh? That's a brilliant idea!

369
00:18:47,126 --> 00:18:49,253
That's the only brilliant idea
you've had tonight!

370
00:18:49,336 --> 00:18:50,754
- Well done!
- Oh! Good night!

371
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:53,132
- Let's go to bed! [SCREAMS]
- Good night!

372
00:18:53,215 --> 00:18:54,758
- Good night!
- Good night!

373
00:18:56,885 --> 00:19:02,933
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

374
00:19:17,906 --> 00:19:24,830
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

375
00:19:35,799 --> 00:19:37,342
[DOOR CREAKS]

376
00:19:41,722 --> 00:19:48,562
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

377
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:09,708
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:20:23,889 --> 00:20:30,771
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

379
00:20:44,910 --> 00:20:46,787
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

380
00:20:46,870 --> 00:20:48,538
[MUSIC STOPS ABRUPTLY]

381
00:20:50,540 --> 00:20:56,421
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:07,057
Dude?

383
00:21:07,140 --> 00:21:08,267
Everything okay?

384
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:10,477
Yeah. I've checked
the user interface flow.

385
00:21:10,560 --> 00:21:13,689
There was just a minor bug,
but I already fixed it.

386
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:14,982
- Okay.
- It's running lag-free.

387
00:21:15,065 --> 00:21:16,650
- We're good to go.
- You sure?

388
00:21:16,733 --> 00:21:17,818
Yeah.

389
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,697
By the way,

390
00:21:21,780 --> 00:21:23,991
I followed up with the police
the other day.

391
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:25,409
Mm-hmm?

392
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:27,369
Unfortunately,

393
00:21:27,452 --> 00:21:31,164
the CCTV cameras around
Caloy's area weren't working,

394
00:21:31,248 --> 00:21:35,127
and they couldn't trace
the number that contacted him.

395
00:21:36,545 --> 00:21:38,005
Sorry, dude.

396
00:21:38,088 --> 00:21:40,799
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

397
00:21:40,882 --> 00:21:43,635
I've already invested
a lot of money into this, dude.

398
00:21:44,303 --> 00:21:45,512
Are you worried?

399
00:21:45,595 --> 00:21:49,349
That LoveLine<i></i>might become a target
once it takes off?

400
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,143
What do you mean, "once it takes off?"

401
00:21:51,226 --> 00:21:53,979
I just know LoveLine will work.

402
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:59,568
We just have to be more prepared
and more careful.

403
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:00,694
It's nothing.

404
00:22:01,695 --> 00:22:03,780
I'm fine. Don't blame yourself, dude.

405
00:22:06,867 --> 00:22:08,452
Auntie, Oli, say hi to the vlog first!

406
00:22:08,535 --> 00:22:09,786
- Hello!
- Hi!

407
00:22:09,870 --> 00:22:11,371
We'll head over there first, okay?

408
00:22:11,455 --> 00:22:12,539
- Sure, Auntie.
- Bye!

409
00:22:12,622 --> 00:22:13,999
- Bye!
- See you.

410
00:22:16,585 --> 00:22:17,878
So here it is,

411
00:22:17,961 --> 00:22:20,297
the biggest plot twist of LoveList.

412
00:22:20,380 --> 00:22:21,715
LoveLine!

413
00:22:21,798 --> 00:22:24,509
A helpline for the brokenhearted.

414
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:27,929
It's our in-app dating coach
and support feature.

415
00:22:28,013 --> 00:22:31,558
At LoveList, we believe that
no woman should ever

416
00:22:31,641 --> 00:22:33,769
have to go through heartbreak alone.

417
00:22:34,519 --> 00:22:36,813
This is your venting-out corner.

418
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:40,067
A safe space for everyone.

419
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:44,321
If you're looking for free therapy,
this is it.

420
00:22:44,404 --> 00:22:45,655
Right, chief?

421
00:22:45,739 --> 00:22:47,699
[BILLY] Yes. Hold on.

422
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:50,786
This is a space where you can reach out,

423
00:22:50,869 --> 00:22:52,746
be helped, be heard.

424
00:22:52,829 --> 00:22:55,248
<i>When it hurts, this is where you come.</i>

425
00:22:55,332 --> 00:22:56,541
[PHONE RINGING]

426
00:22:56,625 --> 00:22:58,835
Hi. Thank you for calling LoveLine,

427
00:22:58,919 --> 00:23:02,089
your safe space for honest
and heart-to-heart conversation.

428
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:03,757
How can I support you today?

429
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,801
I'm a widow.

430
00:23:05,884 --> 00:23:08,386
I met John on LoveList.

431
00:23:08,470 --> 00:23:12,390
[WOMAN] <i>He's so sweet and caring.</i>

432
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:14,142
<i>The problem is,</i>

433
00:23:14,226 --> 00:23:16,853
he lost his job.

434
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:19,689
Should I lend him money?

435
00:23:19,773 --> 00:23:22,526
Noreen, not yet.

436
00:23:23,401 --> 00:23:25,779
Especially if your relationship
is still new

437
00:23:25,862 --> 00:23:28,031
and he's already asking for money.

438
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:33,245
See first if he's still sincere
even when you can't give him anything.

439
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:35,705
His reaction will be very telling.

440
00:23:35,789 --> 00:23:37,457
So be discerning, okay?

441
00:23:37,999 --> 00:23:39,084
Mm-hmm.

442
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:40,418
Thank you.

443
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:42,003
- Okay, good job.
- Chief!

444
00:23:42,087 --> 00:23:42,963
Yes?

445
00:23:44,005 --> 00:23:45,590
This caller seems to know you.

446
00:23:46,216 --> 00:23:47,467
Me?

447
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,468
Hello?

448
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:50,387
Hi, this is Billy speaking.

449
00:23:50,470 --> 00:23:51,721
How can I support you today?

450
00:23:51,805 --> 00:23:54,224
Oh my gosh, Ms. Billy!
Is that really you?

451
00:23:54,307 --> 00:23:55,767
I'm so sorry!

452
00:23:55,851 --> 00:23:58,103
When someone answered earlier,
I thought it was you,

453
00:23:58,186 --> 00:23:59,396
so I said, "Ms. Billy,"

454
00:23:59,479 --> 00:24:01,022
but it turned out
it was one of your agents.

455
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:02,774
Then they suddenly called you.

456
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:05,735
I'm so sorry.
Am I bothering you, Ms. Billy?

457
00:24:05,819 --> 00:24:07,737
Abi, it's you.

458
00:24:08,321 --> 00:24:09,781
Um…

459
00:24:10,824 --> 00:24:12,075
Not at all.

460
00:24:12,617 --> 00:24:15,036
[ABI] <i>I just wanted to congratulate you.</i>

461
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:16,538
Congratulations!

462
00:24:16,621 --> 00:24:18,874
I just wanted to make sure this was real.

463
00:24:18,957 --> 00:24:21,042
I thought maybe I'd be talking to a bot,

464
00:24:21,126 --> 00:24:23,003
but it turns out
it's a real person answering.

465
00:24:23,086 --> 00:24:24,713
That's amazing. Congratulations!

466
00:24:24,796 --> 00:24:25,839
A bot?

467
00:24:25,922 --> 00:24:27,424
How'd you know about that?

468
00:24:27,507 --> 00:24:33,263
Well, Ms. Billy, we own an internet café.

469
00:24:33,346 --> 00:24:35,557
So I know a little about those things.

470
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:37,309
We also have a repair shop.

471
00:24:37,392 --> 00:24:40,395
You know, for fixing gadgets and stuff.

472
00:24:40,478 --> 00:24:41,730
Oh, okay.

473
00:24:42,480 --> 00:24:44,065
Abi, thanks for your support,

474
00:24:44,149 --> 00:24:46,193
but I have to end the call now.

475
00:24:46,276 --> 00:24:48,320
We've got a lot of callers today.

476
00:24:48,403 --> 00:24:52,824
If you ever have time,
just drop by the office.

477
00:24:52,908 --> 00:24:54,910
[SQUEALS] Really?

478
00:24:54,993 --> 00:24:56,036
Okay, Ms. Billy!

479
00:24:56,119 --> 00:24:57,495
I'll definitely look forward to it.

480
00:24:57,579 --> 00:24:58,914
Congratulations again!

481
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:00,832
You're amazing, idol!

482
00:25:00,916 --> 00:25:03,001
Okay. Thank you, Abi. Bye!

483
00:25:04,586 --> 00:25:05,545
Okay.

484
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:06,588
Okay.

485
00:25:07,797 --> 00:25:14,679
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

486
00:25:29,569 --> 00:25:35,325
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

487
00:25:35,408 --> 00:25:37,118
[DOOR CREAKS]

488
00:25:38,954 --> 00:25:42,457
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

489
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:45,543
[SQUEALING]

490
00:25:46,628 --> 00:25:49,172
This room is so beautiful!

491
00:25:50,340 --> 00:25:52,509
This bed is gorgeous!

492
00:25:56,554 --> 00:26:01,518
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

493
00:26:01,601 --> 00:26:02,727
[GROANS]

494
00:26:05,272 --> 00:26:06,731
It's so soft!

495
00:26:06,815 --> 00:26:08,149
This feels amazing!

496
00:26:09,442 --> 00:26:10,819
[EXHALES DEEPLY]

497
00:26:11,778 --> 00:26:13,488
Must be nice.

498
00:26:14,281 --> 00:26:20,328
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

499
00:26:27,085 --> 00:26:29,129
<i>I feel a sense of…</i>

500
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:30,630
<i>Potential? Connection?</i>

501
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:33,300
<i>Auntie, have you seen</i>
<i>my red shoes?</i>

502
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:35,302
[PRECIOUS]<i> First,</i>
<i>you lost your keys.</i>

503
00:26:35,385 --> 00:26:36,678
<i>Now, it's your shoes.</i>

504
00:26:36,761 --> 00:26:38,388
<i>Someone's looking</i>
<i>for you downstairs.</i>

505
00:26:38,471 --> 00:26:40,015
<i>But she doesn't have</i>
<i>an appointment.</i>

506
00:26:40,098 --> 00:26:42,434
<i>Do you think I could be</i>
<i>part of LoveList?</i>

507
00:26:42,517 --> 00:26:43,727
<i>Who bailed you out?</i>

508
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:46,187
<i>How many times</i>
<i>do I have to tell you both?</i>

509
00:26:46,271 --> 00:26:47,981
<i>I don't even know</i>
<i>who my boss is!</i>

510
00:26:48,064 --> 00:26:50,775
<i>If you say anything to that man,</i>
<i>I'll finish you off!</i>

511
00:26:50,859 --> 00:26:52,402
<i>- Caloy!</i>
<i>- And your family--</i>

512
00:26:53,028 --> 00:26:54,487
[BLOWS LANDING]

513
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,448
<i>Who's your boss?</i>

514
00:26:56,531 --> 00:26:57,907
<i>I'd never put you in danger.</i>

515
00:26:57,991 --> 00:26:59,784
<i>- Hello?</i>
<i>- Benilda?</i>

516
00:27:00,452 --> 00:27:01,328
<i>Sweetie?</i>

517
00:27:02,162 --> 00:27:06,499
[PRECIOUS] <i>Billy, why do you think</i>
<i>he suddenly called you?</i>

518
00:27:06,583 --> 00:27:08,293
<i>Let's check out the people</i>
<i>boxing over there.</i>

519
00:27:08,376 --> 00:27:09,336
[JORDAN] <i>I'll teach you.</i>
